READING RULE FOR THE THESIS
  CITE NESTED_CV_AUTHORITATIVE.csv for every nested-CV figure. This script
  reads it; it does not recompute it. There is one implementation (16d).
  Report the NESTED-CV comparison, not the locked-panel training numbers.
  The nested comparison is between two PROCEDURES and is leakage-free; the
  locked 'Train (apparent)' rows are optimistic by construction and are
  labelled as such in the output.
  If the DeLong test shows no significant difference, the correct sentence
  is: 'excluding the MHC did not measurably reduce diagnostic performance,
  so the panel does not depend on HLA linkage disequilibrium'. That is a
  STRENGTH of the MHC-free panel, and it is the version to carry forward.
  Every Male row remains EXPLORATORY at n = 38/13/9 regardless of AUC.

